# Build on A2A Cloud

This agent runs on **A2A Cloud**. Full API reference is in `AGENTS.md` at the
project root — read it. This skill is the step-by-step playbook.

## Add a skill

1. Open `agent.py`. Add an `async` method on the agent class decorated with
   `@a2a.tool(description="...")`. The description is what the model reads to
   decide when to call the skill — make it specific.
2. Type every parameter (they become the input schema) and the return value.
3. First arg after `self` is always `ctx: RunContext[<AuthModel>]`.

```python
@a2a.tool(description="Summarize text into N bullet points")
async def summarize(self, ctx: RunContext[NoAuth], text: str, n: int = 3) -> str:
    creds = ctx.llm
    if not creds.api_key:
        return "LLM key required — add an LLM credential in Settings > LLM credentials."
    await ctx.emit_progress(f"summarizing {len(text)} chars")
    ...
```

## The four things you'll wire

- **LLM**: `ctx.llm` → `LLMCreds(model, api_key, source)`. Only sanctioned
  credential. Never read `OPENAI_API_KEY`, `A2A_LITELLM_KEY`, or provider keys;
  never fake a fallback. Guard on empty `api_key`.
- **Durable files**: `ctx.workspace_backend()`, `ctx.write_artifact(...)`, or
  `ctx.workspace`. Write intentional outputs to `/workspace/outputs/...`.
- **Running code / CLIs**: `await ctx.workspace_shell(cmd, image="python:3.11-slim", timeout_seconds=120)`.
  Not a plain subprocess — that output isn't durable.
- **DeepAgents graph**: `create_a2a_deep_agent(ctx, creds=ctx.llm, backend=ctx.workspace_backend(), tools=[...], system_prompt=...)`, invoke with `config={"recursion_limit": 500}`.

## Verify before shipping

```bash
a2a validate                                                  # agent loads, no errors
a2a card                                                      # card schema is well-formed
a2a test --invoke --skill <name> --args-json '{"...":"..."}'  # exercise the new skill
a2a deploy                                                    # ship it
```

If `a2a validate` fails, fix the load error before anything else — the platform
build will reject a card that doesn't compile.

## Common mistakes

- Reading a provider key instead of `ctx.llm` → violates platform policy; will
  not have a key in production anyway.
- Writing files with `open()`/`asyncio` subprocess → not durable, vanishes after
  the request. Use the workspace backend or sandbox.
- Vague `@a2a.tool` description → the model can't route to the skill.
- Forgetting `config={"recursion_limit": 500}` on DeepAgents `ainvoke`.
